{{/*
views.gohtml — the view list: every page orbital derives from the deployed schema.

A SETTINGS page, so it follows approval-policies.gohtml (heading + description +
table) rather than servers.gohtml (tabs bar, no heading). Those are the house's
two list patterns and they are not interchangeable: a record list identifies
itself by the active nav item, a settings page states what it is.

Rows come from GET /api/v1/views via JS, not from the handler. Orbital's UI is a
first-class consumer of its own public API (CLAUDE.md), so this page reads the
same endpoint orbctl and AEP would — a private server-side path would let the
two drift.

READ-ONLY today. Editing a view is the P1 override layer (Postgres deltas,
admin-only, audited); the Source column exists now and gains the value
"overridden" then, rather than appearing later.
*/}}
{{define "page"}}
  <main class="app-main-grid">
    <div class="app-menu">
      {{template "menu.gohtml" .}}
    </div>
    <div class="app-main p-5">
      {{if not .IsAuthn}}
        {{template "login-gate.gohtml" .}}
      {{else}}

      <p class="is-size-4 mb-2" data-testid="page-heading">Views</p>
      <p class="has-text-grey page-description">Every page orbital derives from the deployed schema.</p>

      <div id="views-error" class="notification is-danger is-light" style="display:none;"></div>

      <table class="table is-striped is-hoverable is-fullwidth is-size-7" id="views-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th></th>
            <th>Slug</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Label</th>
            <th>In nav</th>
            <th>Fields</th>
            <th>Tabs</th>
            <th>Source</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
      </table>

      {{end}}
    </div>
  </main>
{{end}}
